    "title": "John Brown was, and still is, right - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Preston Thomas ’28 ,\n1 days ago On Nov. 2, 1859, abolitionist John Brown was on trial for murder and treason against the Commonwealth of Virginia and an attempt to incite a slave insurrection. When asked if there was any reason the sentence should not be imposed, Brown rose and gave a short, yet profound, speech that still holds much relevance today. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
